  "title": "P-ary m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from Martínez-Cagigal et al. (2023)",
  "description": "This dataset comprises EEG recordings from 16 healthy participants performing a code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) brain-computer interface task using p-ary m-sequences. The study investigates non-binary m-sequence stimulation patterns to enhance user comfort in c-VEP-based BCIs. Data were collected across 5 sessions per subject with 8 runs per session at 256 Hz sampling rate using 16 EEG channels, providing a comprehensive resource for BCI paradigm development and evaluation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired at 256 Hz sampling rate using 16 channels arranged in a standard 1005 montage with 50 Hz line frequency. Participants completed 5 sessions, each containing 8 runs (6 training, 2 testing) of the c-VEP paradigm with 11 visual stimulus classes based on p-ary m-sequences. Trial intervals were 1 second in duration.",
